        {
          "line": 182,
          "text": "and by a CZI EOSS award."
        },
        {
          "line": 183,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 184,
          "text": "## Input data"
        },
        {
          "line": 185,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 186,
          "text": "### Why un-normalized counts?"
        },
        {
          "line": 187,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 188,
          "text": "As input, the DESeq2 package expects count data as obtained, e.g.,"
        },
        {
          "line": 189,
          "text": "from RNA-seq or another high-throughput sequencing experiment, in the form of a"
        },
        {
          "line": 190,
          "text": "matrix of integer values. The value in the *i*-th row and the *j*-th column of"
        },
        {
          "line": 191,
          "text": "the matrix tells how many reads can be assigned to gene *i* in sample *j*."
        },
        {
          "line": 192,
          "text": "Analogously, for other types of assays, the rows of the matrix might correspond"
        },
        {
          "line": 193,
          "text": "e.g. to binding regions (with ChIP-Seq) or peptide sequences (with"
        },
        {
          "line": 194,
          "text": "quantitative mass spectrometry). We will list method for obtaining count matrices"
        },
        {
          "line": 195,
          "text": "in sections below."
        },
        {
          "line": 196,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 197,
          "text": "The values in the matrix should be un-normalized counts or estimated"
        },
        {
          "line": 198,
          "text": "counts of sequencing reads (for"
        },
        {
          "line": 199,
          "text": "single-end RNA-seq) or fragments (for paired-end RNA-seq). "
        },
        {
          "line": 200,
          "text": "The [RNA-seq workflow](http://www.bioconductor.org/help/workflows/rnaseqGene/)"
        },
        {
          "line": 201,
          "text": "describes multiple techniques for preparing such count matrices.  It"
        },
        {
          "line": 202,
          "text": "is important to provide count matrices as input for DESeq2's"
        },
        {
          "line": 203,
          "text": "statistical model [@Love2014] to hold, as only the count values allow"
        },
        {
          "line": 204,
          "text": "assessing the measurement precision correctly. The DESeq2 model"
        },
        {
          "line": 205,
          "text": "internally corrects for library size, so transformed or normalized"
        },
        {
          "line": 206,
          "text": "values such as counts scaled by library size should not be used as"
        },
        {
          "line": 207,
          "text": "input."
        },
        {
          "line": 208,
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
